 "narrative": "The new block largely confirms a context-modified feature_063 association and mostly rejects other proposed interactions. H105 and H103 are the key results. H105 directly tests feature_063=1 versus 0 within the accepted feature_037=0/feature_010=0 stratum restricted to high feature_038. The signed estimate is +0.538 with signed interval +0.402 to +0.674, corresponding to a raw feature_063=1 versus 0 difference of about -0.538 composite dependency-score units. This is far beyond the 0.15-unit threshold, has adequately powered cells (77/522), and supports accepting H105. It extends the already accepted residual-stratum high-feature_038 result H93 to the broader H87 context. H94, the low-feature_038 complement in the residual stratum, is near null: signed estimate -0.020, signed interval -0.089 to +0.049. There is no evidence of a meaningful negative feature_063 effect in low feature_038, so H94 is rejected and closed. H103 formalizes the high-versus-low feature_038 interaction in the broader H87 stratum: signed estimate +0.520, signed interval +0.357 to +0.683. Because the whole interval is beyond the threshold in the claimed negative-interaction direction, the feature_063 lower-outcome association is materially stronger in high feature_038 than in low feature_038 within the feature_037=0/feature_010=0 context. I accept H103 and keep it active; it is the most decision-relevant new interaction result, so I request validation for H103 rather than for overlapping sparse subgroup contrasts.\n\nThe other standardized-signature interactions do not support the hypothesized direction. H107, testing feature_036 context, is null-to-mildly opposite: signed estimate -0.054, signed interval -0.232 to +0.124. There is no evidence of a meaningful negative feature_063-by-feature_036 interaction, so it is rejected and closed. H106, testing feature_018 in the claimed high-feature_018-stronger direction, is actually entirely on the opposite side: signed estimate -0.272, signed interval -0.445 to -0.099. This rejects H106 as stated. The reversed interval would be +0.272 (+0.099 to +0.445), indicating that feature_063 is probably associated with lower outcome_001 more strongly in low feature_018 than in high feature_018, although the reversed interval's lower bound is below the 0.15 threshold. I registered a reversed feature_018 interaction claim and direct high/low feature_018 comparisons in the H87 stratum for later refinement.\n\nThe long log_pfs_months interaction H104 does not support a broad long-PFS-specific feature_063 context: signed estimate +0.028, signed interval -0.211 to +0.266. This tempers interpretation of the accepted but sparse residual long-PFS stratum H92; the feature_063 effect is not clearly modified by long log-PFS in the broader H87 stratum. H104 is rejected and closed.\n\nFormal attenuation interactions by dominant binary predictors remain inconclusive. H108 (feature_010=1 versus 0 within feature_037=0) and H109 (feature_037=1 versus 0 within feature_010=0) have positive points (+0.092 and +0.094) consistent with attenuation, but their intervals include null and threshold values: -0.230 to +0.413 and -0.091 to +0.278, respectively. They are unresolved and deferred. Direct claims H69 and H70 already found no meaningful negative feature_063 association when feature_037=1 or feature_010=1 broadly, so the attenuation hypothesis is plausible, but these formal interactions are not decisive.\n\nThe dominant-marker additivity block mostly supports approximate additivity. H40, H44, and H45 have near-null interaction estimates and are rejected/closed. H41 is different: the feature_002 interaction with feature_010=1 is +0.210, signed interval +0.019 to +0.400. The point exceeds the threshold, but the interval includes subthreshold magnitudes, so it remains unresolved. I keep H41 active as a possible non-additive feature_002-by-feature_010 signal, but it is secondary to the feature_063 context questions. I reassessed H93 as accepted and closed because H105, H103, and H94 now place the residual high-feature_038 finding in a broader context; the direct high-feature_038 association remains accepted, while the interaction is being validated separately. All conclusions remain descriptive associations in this supplied dataset, not causal, biological, mechanistic, or generalizable claims.",
 "research_notes": "Current accepted central supplied-dataset associations: feature_037=1 lowers outcome_001; feature_002=1 and feature_010=1 raise outcome_001; feature_063=1 lowers outcome_001 when feature_010 is absent and especially when feature_037 and feature_010 are both absent (H87/H61/H90/H92/H95/H96). New accepted context: within feature_037=0/feature_010=0, the feature_063 negative association is strong when feature_038>=0 (H105; direct raw about -0.538) and formal high-vs-low feature_038 interaction is strong (H103; signed +0.520 [0.357,0.683]). Low-feature_038 complement H94 is null, so H105/H103/H94 jointly support feature_038 context modification in the H87 stratum. H103 is under requested validation. Do not overclaim: H104 says broad long logPFS does not meaningfully modify feature_063 in the broader H87 stratum; H107 rejects feature_036 context; H106 as stated rejects feature_018 high-context but supports a reversed feature_018 pattern that needs a new claim (registered). Feature_010/feature_037 attenuation interactions H108/H109 are only suggestive and deferred. Dominant-marker additivity: H40/H44/H45 mostly additive, H41 possible feature_002-by-feature_010 positive interaction unresolved active. Next priorities: (1) assess H103 validation; (2) analyze reversed feature_018 interaction and direct high/low feature_018 comparisons in H87 stratum; (3) run logPFS robustness H97-H102 for central markers if capacity allows; (4) follow up H41 only if it remains central after higher-priority feature_063 work. Keep low-priority residual flag screens H80-H86 deferred unless a specific scientific question justifies them. All conclusions are descriptive dataset associations, not causal, biological, mechanistic, or generalizable.",
